body:
Following #408 we had an idea with @Jerskouille to allow the toggle to be really usable in various toggling situations.

We can add "on value" and "off value" feature to the current toggle API.

Handle "free\_shipping" being either `true` or nothing (nothing = free + non free shipping)

```js
toggle({
  facetName: 'free_shipping',
  values: {
    on: true
  }
})
```

Handle "archived" being either `true` or `false`:

```js
toggle({
  facetName: 'archived',
  values: {
    on: true
    off: false
  }
})
```

Handle "fruit" being `banana` or `oranges`:

```js
toggle({
  facetName: 'fruit',
  values: {
    on: 'banana',
    off: 'orange'
  }
})
```

Handle "only my favorites" or "everything":

```js
toggle({
  facetName: '_tags',
  values: {
    on: 'user42'
  }
})
```

Be careful about the default count we send, it's right now not accurate (showing "false" values instead of true)
